<CLAIM evidence_lines="9, 14, 15">
mechanism: The lookup result `entry` is obtained under the pm lock (line 9), but the lock is released at line 12 before `entry` is dereferenced again at lines 14-15 to check `entry->addr.id` and to call `sk_stop_timer_sync(sk, &entry->add_timer)`. Between the unlock and use, another thread can free or reuse the entry (e.g., via mptcp_pm_remove_add_addr or similar paths that delete the anno list entry), causing a use-after-free on `entry->addr.id` and on `entry->add_timer`.
</CLAIM>

