<CLAIM evidence_lines="19, 20, 21, 27, 28, 29, 43">
mechanism: After xa_alloc succeeds at line 19, several early-return error paths (lines 21, 29) return without calling xa_erase/xa_free on liteuart_array, leaving the allocated entry permanently occupying the index and leaking the xarray slot; additionally, if uart_add_one_port fails at line 43, the xarray entry is also not removed. The externally controlled alias id (line 9) determines which slot is consumed, so a failed probe permanently blocks that port id.
